      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LANGDOWN LEGACY (2) is edging towards his first win, and battled away well enough for second at Toowoomba just over 3 weeks ago. If he can cope with this unique track for the first time, then he is an each-way player again. HE'S A FIGHTER (1) whacked away for third at Dalby last start over 1400m, and he will be peaking at the right time for his first attempt over 1600m. He has the pole position, and can take this out. SWEEDISH QUEEN (9) has improved in each of her runs back from a spell, and racing over 1500m for the first time should suit her. Keep safe. SHAWNEE BOY (5) resumes from a spell, and should be a lot stronger this season. He ran the odd good race earlier in the year, and should be hitting the line hard late in this.",
